 ],
 "notes": "Long two-storey bar on a ridge above the valley, the view side (balcony, lawn) taken as south. From the long lawn elevation (stone ground floor set back behind concrete columns, a continuous cantilevered floor slab with beam ends and a steel rail, the upper floor glazed between concrete piers, a thin cantilevered roof with beam stubs along its edge, the board-formed concrete chimney), the back elevation (the upper storey a closed concrete band with large punched windows and a strip of low windows, stone below), the west-end view (the roof and floor cantilevered over an open corner terrace, a tall concrete blade rising past the roof) and the cactus-garden view (gravel path along the stone base, a concrete blade panel standing off the east end). Length (~45 m) and heights scaled from a person against the lawn elevation; depth (~10 m), the positions of ground-floor openings and the open covered bay at the east end are estimated. The stone is the 'stone' material standing in for the rounded fieldstone masonry. Planting reduced to a lawn with a stone edge, gravel, a few trees and columnar cacti."
}